36,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The timing shows a full pass takes over an hour and a half. More concerning is that our standards for ""done"" vary wildly, which explains why the cleanliness of the rooms is so inconsistent.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"My findings suggest a significant imbalance. Some of us are away for weeks at a time, yet the kitchen mess is primarily generated by only a few of us. The current ""equal"" split seems logically flawed.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"I knew it! The bathroom gets dirty so fast because there's barely any air in there, and some people just wipe the sink and call it a day! No wonder it feels so different every time!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems we have some confusion with our supplies, as we are buying things twice. Also, the management office offers a cleaner, though the billing is handled by one person. Perhaps we can find a way to make this simpler.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It is telling that our past conflicts stem from reminders of undone work. Furthermore, the previous tenants warned that permanent assignments led to silence and distance. We must choose a path that avoids such rigidity.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, if the usage is concentrated among a few, a simple rotation might still feel unfair. However, @Servas, if permanent roles cause resentment, we must be careful. We need a system that balances actual effort and usage.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely, @Minako. If we ignore the fact that some contribute more to the mess while others are absent, we are merely substituting one form of unfairness for another. Logic suggests the workload should reflect actual usage.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"But if we just do it based on who uses it, will we still fight? I just want it to be clean! Maybe a professional cleaner would be better so we don't have to argue about the grout?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"That is a lovely thought, Sakura. A professional might bring a wonderful sense of order, and it would certainly stop us from worrying about who is paying for the spray or the sponges.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Servas,,"While a professional would bring order, we must consider the cost and the spirit of our home. If we outsource everything, do we lose the opportunity to care for our space and each other? Let us weigh the options carefully.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Servas, I value the spirit of the home, but the data shows we are spending over an hour and a half on a full pass. If we can't agree on standards, we're just wasting time.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, I concur. When standards are subjective and usage is skewed, a manual rotation becomes a catalyst for friction rather than a solution. We need a system that removes the ambiguity of ""done.""","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"I agree! If we have a professional, they'll know exactly how to clean the grout and the drains, and we won't have to guess if it's actually clean or not!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"It would be such a relief for everyone. If we have a professional, we can focus on our friendship instead of the bills and the cleaning supplies. It seems like a very peaceful way to live.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Servas,,"I hear your longing for peace, and it is a powerful argument. If a professional removes the burden of reminders and the ambiguity of standards, it may indeed be the bridge that keeps us all speaking and smiling.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Minako,,It seems we have reached a consensus that removing the ambiguity of standards and the burden of manual labor is our priority. Let us move to the final round and see which option best fits these needs.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
